OL,4,CResidents could face second 8.99%      
OL,5,Ccouncil tax rise                       
OL,6,GResidents could face a second          
OL,7,Gconsecutive council tax rise of 8.99%  
OL,8,Gafter Shropshire Council was advised   
OL,9,Gto seek another increase above the     
OL,10,Gusual limit.                           
OL,12,FThe authority increased its share of   
OL,13,Fbills by 8.99% in April after          
OL,14,Freceiving rare government permission   
OL,15,Fto exceed the normal cap on council    
OL,16,Ftax rises.                             
OL,18,FA recently published finance report    
OL,19,Fhas recommended that council tax       
OL,20,Fshould be raised again "to the maximum 
OL,21,Fpossible level" permitted by the       
OL,22,Fgovernment in 2027-28.            G3/4 
OL,23,D]CNews IndexG102CFlashG150CRegionalG160
